    death(){ tone(90,0.3,'sawtooth',0.12); },
    gold(){ /* 2026-10-08: sparkly — a quick rising glitter of bell tones */ tone(1568,0.07,'triangle',0.09); tone(2093,0.08,'sine',0.08,0.035); tone(2637,0.09,'sine',0.07,0.07); tone(3136,0.12,'sine',0.055,0.105); tone(4186,0.18,'sine',0.035,0.14); tone(3520,0.16,'sine',0.03,0.2); },
    // Card unlocking (2026-09-22, style-guide enforcement pass): a brand-new card is a bigger,
    // rarer reward moment than the routine "level up a card you already own" pack outcome, but
    // both were calling the exact same shared starFallVfx.celebrate() -> SoundKit.gold() "cha-
    // ching" — genuinely indistinguishable audio for two mechanically very different outcomes,
    // which is exactly what style-guideline.md section 5/checklist item 4 calls out ("don't reuse
    // an existing tone for a new mechanic just because it's 'close enough'"). A rising 3-note
