// Generic card-unlock mechanic (2026-09-25, per explicit request: "you can unlock cards when
// certain things happen. Oh, and of course, if you get a card reward e.g. reward from an event
// or skirmish, it's also unlocked" — deliberately framed by the request as "available but not
// wired"). Today the only two things that ever grant a real unlock are a Shop pack's unlock roll
// (buyPack below) and finishing the tutorial series (grantTutorialSeriesRewards below) — both
// already reached straight into myUnlockedCardIds themselves before this existed. This is the
// single, generic entry point every FUTURE unlock condition (an achievement, a milestone, a new
// event/skirmish reward type — none of which exist yet) should call instead of touching
// myUnlockedCardIds directly, so "grant a permanent unlock" is always one call, always logged the
// same way, and can never forget the save+cloud-push step. The two existing call sites are now
// routed through it too (see their own updated comments) — not because they were broken, but so
// this is the ONE real code path an unlock ever goes through, ready for whatever "certain things
