// inserted directly into the live board row at exactly the DOM position a real play would land
// it (see placeCard() in bramblewood-engine.js: new cards always push() onto the end of their
// flank array, and row.left renders REVERSED — see rowHTML's `[...rows.left].reverse()` — so
// the newest left-flank card is always the FAR/outer one, i.e. the first DOM child; the newest
// right-flank card is always the outer/last DOM child; center just replaces the empty-slot
// placeholder directly). Because it's a real DOM insertion into the actual flex row rather than
// a separately-drawn overlay, the browser's own layout does the "existing cards shift to make
