// that instant reflow into an animated slide, exactly like a real play does.
// Bugfix (2026-09-17, found via a real end-to-end playtest — "placement/movement should
// depend on where the card is right now, not be static"): the Left/Right button hover
// highlight below (row-dragover/drag-side-*) was being driven purely off 'mouseenter'/
// 'mouseleave' events. That desyncs from reality whenever the row underneath a MOTIONLESS
// cursor gets rebuilt — which happens after every single round, via resolveRound()'s final
// renderMatchUI() — because Chromium recomputes :hover state on that DOM swap and fires a
// synthetic 'mouseenter' on whichever fresh element now sits under the pointer, even though
// the user's mouse never actually moved. With no real mousemove to ever pair it with a
// 'mouseleave', that highlight then froze "on" for the rest of the match — a highlight
