  try{ fxHook('boardRendered', matchState); }catch(e){} // FX batch B (2026-10-15): who can't see in the dark, the forecast pill
  try{ syncTideScene(matchState); }catch(e){} // the standing Tide: the wet look on new cards (2026-10-18)
  try{ syncUnitLightPools(); }catch(e){} // unit light in the dark (2026-10-15)
  // Bugfix (2026-09-17, root cause of the residual small stuck-transform matrices test_v24
  // still caught after the scale-1.08/shove fixes above — e.g. a card left mid fall-in at
  // `matrix(0.68, -0.07, 0.07, 0.68, 0, -30)`): resolveRound()'s mid-round replay loop already
  // knows to pause briefly after a renderBoard() call that introduced a live spawn, so the
  // entrance animation is actually visible before the round can "finish" (see that pause's own
  // comment, "spawning still does not look animated"). But resolveRound()'s FINAL, always-runs
  // "guaranteed-accurate sync" render — which can itself introduce new elements, e.g. an
  // onDeathSpawn token the progressive replay never modeled — had no equivalent pause: the very
  // next line flips m.resolving to false and re-enables controls in the same tick, so a caller
  // (or a test) that waits only for `resolving===false` can observe that render's brand-new
  // cards still mid-drop, not yet settled. Reporting whether THIS render introduced any new
  // entrants lets resolveRound() give that final render the same courtesy pause.
  try{ evoSyncTargets(); }catch(e){} // Package EV (2026-10-21): the legal bases of a held evolute stay lit across a re-render
  try{ fogSyncLayer(m); }catch(e){} // 2026-10-21 (package FOG): the drifting mist over the out-of-reach enemy columns
