        // could pop in and the round could "finish" (controls re-enabled) before a person's eye
        // even caught the motion.
        //
        // FIXED 2026-09-21 ("Spawning and the movement of the card sometimes collides and messes
        // up. Spawn first, then collapse once the animation is complete"): this used to be a flat
        // `sleep(420)` — a guess that happened to roughly match a single card's entrance at
        // normal speed but fell well short of the tween's REAL total duration (the settle-bounce
        // and per-card stagger were never accounted for — see spawnEntranceSettleMs's own
        // comment), so the loop routinely moved on to the round's NEXT event — another spawn, a
        // collapseIn, or the final sync render — and called renderBoard()/Flip.from() again while
        // this spawn's own entrance tween was still actively mid-flight, which is exactly what
        // read as the animation "colliding" with the next card's movement. Now waits the real,
        // computed settle time for however many cards just landed, respecting current playback
